2 CONT http://www.highbeam.com/doc/1P2-1201240.html
2 CONT
2 CONT Torfinn Oftedal, 80, a retired Norwegian diplomat who had served 17 years in Washington and later as Norwegian ambassador to Austria, Canada, Czechoslovakia and Romania, died of cancer July 2 at a hospital in Baddek, Nova Scotia. 
2 CONC A resident of Washington since retiring in 1975, Mr. Oftedal had been staying at a vacation home at the time of his death.
2 CONT
2 CONT A native of Sandnes, Norway, Mr. Oftedal graduated from the University of Trondheim and entered the Norwegian Foreign Service in 1938. He was assigned in Washington from 1938 to 1946 and again from 1951 to 1960.
2 CONT
2 CONT He had served as Norwegian delegate to the Monetary Conference at Bretton Woods in 1944, the United Nations …
