2 CONT Story on Olaus Olsen Lende Cars:
2 CONT
2 CONT LENDE 1902-1909(?) Granite Falls
2 CONT
2 CONT Olaus Lende began building cars in his machine Shop in Granite Falls in 1902, and by the time he forsook the manufacture of Lendes to be a Studebaker agent, he had built eighteen cars. Lende personally designed and manufactured th
2 CONC e cars, four-Cylinder, air-cooled engines which drove by means of a friction traansmissíon.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1907 dreams of bigger markets led Lende and several other men to begin selling stock in the Lende Automobile Manufacturing Company out of a Minneapolis office. However, a year's effort to sell stock and locate a factory bore no
2 CONC  fruit. In a letter to Lende, an agent lamented, "I was at Farmington again this afternoon and must say that the prospects for doing anything there upon the Proposition we have before them is very doubtful." Back in Granite Falls,
2 CONC  after his unsuccessful venture, Lende probably continued to build vehicles for some years.
2 CONT
2 CONT Info. on the Car:
2 CONT
2 CONT Lende Air Cooled Gasoline Cars. Made by the Lende Automobile Mfg. Co., 617 Guaranty Bldg., Minneapolis, Minn.
2 CONT
2 CONT Lende 30 H. P. Touring CAR. $1800
2 CONT
2 CONT Motor, 4-cylinder, vertical, air-cooled, 4 cycle, 4-1/2x5 inches, 30 H. P., under hood; shaft drive; plain crank shaft bearings; splash lubrication; jump spark ignition by storage battery; cork inserted clutch; planetary change sp
2 CONC eed gear; three speeds forward and one reverse; direct on high; mounted on ball bearings; shaft drive; 103-Inch wheel base; 32x3-1/2-inch tires; roller wheel bearings; wood frame; full-ellipic springs; 2 sets of brakes on rear whe
2 CONC els; two control levers; 18 gallon gasoline tank under front seat; body touring car type; seats 5 persons; full equipment; lamps and horn; price $1800.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
