2 CONT
2 CONT Maiden Name: Gustava Olsdatter Lende Stavanger Norway (Rogaland Co. Norway) Immigrated from Norway to USA Naturalized U.S. Citizen
2 CONT
2 CONT Parents: Ole O. Lende Grethe Marie Kverneland Lende
2 CONT
2 CONT Spouse: Nicolai Pedersen
2 CONT
2 CONT Gustava & Nicolai's Children: (known) Christine Pedersen Ree Grethe Pedersen Paul Nora Pedersen Mossige Oscar Peterson (Pedersen) Ella Pedersen Berdeen Ruth Pedersen Jacobson Nettie Peterson Wait Martin Leonard Peterson (Pedersen)
2 CONC  Sylvia Pedersen Miller George Leroy Peterson (Pedersen) Bergliot Esther Pedersen Larson
2 CONT
2 CONT ( Some children went by Pedersen, others Peterson.)
2 CONT
2 CONT Grandchildren: Valette G. Ree McKibben Alice Leona Ree Kleve
2 CONT
2 CONT (Many Grandchildren and Great Grandchildren.)
2 CONT
2 CONT ********************
2 CONT
2 CONT ** In Loving Memory of Gustava ** Gustava will be missed, loved and remembered forever in the hearts of all who loved her. Gustava Lende was born in Stavanger Norway. Gustava Lende immigrated to America with her Parents when she w
2 CONC as 13 yrs old. Gustava immigrated from Norway abt. 1879. Her Family settled at a farm west of Cottonwood, Lyon County Minnesota USA. Gustava married Nicolai Pedersen in 1886 in Lucas, Lyon Co. MN. Nicolai also immigrated from Norw
2 CONC ay in 1880. They were in the farming industry. Gustava and Nicolai raised their children in Friendship, Yellow Medicine MN. They are survived by many relatives.
2 CONT
2 CONT ------------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Obituary Lynner Funeral Home Clarksfield Minnesota USA
2 CONT
2 CONT Gustava Lende Pedersen Gustava Pedersen passed away June 2, 1953 at the Clarksfield Hospital in Clarksfield Minnesota at age 87 yrs. Gustava was born in Stavanger Norway Feb. 8, 1866 to Ole and Gretha Kverneland Lende. She came wi
2 CONC th her Parents to America when she was 13 yrs old. They settled on a farm in Lyon County Minnesota. In 1886 Gustava was united in  marriage to Nicolai Pedersen and they moved to a farm in Clarkfield MN. There were eleven children 
2 CONC in the family, seven of whom are still living. They are Nora (Mrs. Adolf Mossige) of Cottonwood Minnesota, Oscar, Leonard and Sylvia (Mrs. Lester Miller) of Clarksfield, Nettie (Mrs. Maxwell Wait) of Granite Falls Minnesota, Georg
2 CONC e Pederson of Copenhagen Denmark and Bergilot (Mrs. E.R. Larson) of Anoka Minnesota. There are 23 grandchildren and a number of great grandchildren. One Sister, Mrs. Bertha Mauland survives of the  4 sisters and 3 brothers in the 
2 CONC  Lende Family. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Gustava's Husband Nicolai and four Daughters preceded her in Death.  They were Christine (Mrs. Arnt Ree), Grethe ( Mrs. W.L. Paul), Ella (Mrs. Charles Berdeen) and Ruth (Mrs. Herbert Jacobson)
2 CONT
2 CONT Gustava's Philosophy of Life sustained her through many trials and won her many friends. Blessed be her Memory.
2 CONT
2 CONT Funeral Services Friday June 5, 1953 2:00 PM Spring Creek Lutheran Church Normania Township Yellow Medicine Minnesota
2 CONT
2 CONT Interment- Final Resting Place Spring Creek Lutheran Cemetery
2 CONT
2 CONT Clergy Officiating: Rev. P.S. Mork
2 CONT
2 CONT Vocal Soloist Mrs. Arden Lynne " Mother Knows " "Taenk Naar Engang Hver  Taage er Forsvunden"
2 CONT
2 CONT Pallbearers: Clarence Helmstetter, James Paul, Howard Miller, Clemer Wait, Stanley Jacobson, Erling Mossige
2 CONT
2 CONT *****
2 CONT
2 CONT * * A TRIBUTE TO MOTHER ** A beautiful life has ended, a fine Christian has passed on to a well deserved reward. Mothers life was one of great love and devotion to God and Family. She never thought of self- only of others. Her let
2 CONC ters which came so faithfully even up to the last day, and all other good deeds have now ended, but her teaching and her Christian Spirit will continue to inspire us. Even her letters spoke of the kindness of neighbors and friends
2 CONC . Let us think of Mothers passing on as the triumph ending a full and complete life earth. Tribute written by Children George and Lillian Peterson. Posted on Lynner Funeral Home Obituary site.
2 CONT
2 CONT (Gustava's 1953 Obituary and Tribute  transcribed and paraphrased via  Lynner Funeral Home, Clarksfield MN)
2 CONT
2 CONT -----
2 CONT
2 CONT Minnesota Marriage Records: Gustava Lende Marriage to Nicolai Pedersen  Jan. 25, 1886 Lucus, Lyon Co. MN Certificate: 1255713
2 CONT
2 CONT --
2 CONT
2 CONT Some references to Gustava being born in Rogaland Norway. Per Gustava's  Obituary, Gustava Lende was born in Stavenger Norway, now being called Rogaland Norway.
2 CONT
2 CONT --
2 CONT
2 CONT U.S. Evangelical Church of Lutheran of America records site: Nicolai Pedersen married Gustava Lende Jan. 25, 1886 Cottonwood Hanley Falls MN Yellow Medicine Lutheran Church Hanley Falls, MN.
2 CONT
2 CONT Sites Nicolai's Parents as Napoleon Pedersen and Argel James Jensen (sp)
2 CONT
2 CONT Sites Gustava Lende's Parents Ole O. Lende and Gretta Lende (Grethe)
2 CONT
