2 CONT
2 CONT Bertha Maria Lende Mauland BIRTH	3 May 1870 Time, Time kommune, Rogaland fylke, Norway DEATH	6 Sep 1959 (aged 89) Lyon County, Minnesota, USA BURIAL	 Saint Lucas Cemetery Normania, Yellow Medicine County, Minnesota, USA
2 CONT
2 CONT Family Members
2 CONT
2 CONT Parents Ole O Lende 1833–1903
2 CONT
2 CONT Grethe Marie Kverneland Lende 1837–1923
2 CONT
2 CONT Spouse Tollef T Mauland 1864–1942
2 CONT
2 CONT Siblings Martha Lende 1864–1896
2 CONT
2 CONT Gustava Lende Pedersen 1866–1953
2 CONT
2 CONT Gabriel Olous Lende 1868–1953
2 CONT
2 CONT Ola Lende 1876–1893
2 CONT
2 CONT Children Elizabeth Mauland Huso 1891–1991
2 CONT
2 CONT Oscar T Mauland 1893–1987
2 CONT
2 CONT Ternys Reynold Mauland 1895–1978
2 CONT
2 CONT Conrad Milfred Mauland 1897–1974
2 CONT
2 CONT Thomas Bernhard Mauland 1900–1990
2 CONT
2 CONT Bertha Marie Mauland was born May 3, 1870, at Time, Jaeren, near Stavanger, Norway, the daughter of Ola and Grethe (Kverneland) Lende. She was baptized into the Christian faith in the Time Church. At the age of nine years, she imm
2 CONC igrated with her family to America, settling on a farm west of Cottonwood. She was confirmed at the Yellow Medicine Lutheran Church west of Hanley Falls by Rev. Knute Thorstenson. On December 27, 1890, she was united in marriage t
2 CONC o Tollef Mauland at Silo Lutheran Church in Cottonwood by Rev. Thorstenson. They settled on a farm southwest of Cottonwood where she lived the remainder of her life except for ten years residence in the Normania community. To this
2 CONC  union were born six children: Elizabeth (Mrs. Alfred Huso), Oscar, Conrad, Bernhard of Cottonwood, Reynold of Clarkfield and Grethe (Mrs. Henry Foss) of Echo.
2 CONT
2 CONT Mrs. Mauland passed away on Sunday, September 6, 1959, at the home of her daughter, Mrs. Elizabeth Huso, at the age of 89 years, 4 months and 3 days. She was the last member of her family and one of the last pioneers in the St. Lu
2 CONC cas community where she resided for almost 80 years.
2 CONT
2 CONT She is survived by her six children, thirteen grandchildren and twenty-six great grandchildren.
2 CONT
2 CONT She was preceded in death by her husband, who passed away in 1942, her parents, three brothers, four sisters, two sons-in-law, one daughter-in-law and two grandsons.
