1 NOTE {geni:about_me} === GEDCOM Note ===
2 CONT {\rtf1\ansi\ansicpg1252\cocoartf1343\cocoasubrtf160{\fonttbl\f0\fswiss\fcharset0 Helvetica;}{\colortbl;\red255\green255\blue255;}\pard\tx560\tx1120\tx1680\tx2240\tx2800\tx3360\tx3920\tx4480\tx5040\tx5600\tx6160\tx6720\pardirnatura
2 CONC l\f0\fs24 \cf0 It was at 1954 Williams Secondary, Grants Pass, Oregon that behind the house in the back acreage, there was a great swamp and many wild animals could be found there. (This is Lanny talking) Apparently, Denny was dir
2 CONC ected by Grandpa to fill that swamp with a "Gibson" tractor.  In his inexperience, he entered the swamp too far and stuck the tractor. He begged for Lanny's assistance so that Grandpa wouldn't find out about his inadequate driving
2 CONC  experience. Finally Denny had to wade into the swamp to try and lift out the front blade while having Lanny put the tractor in gear to try to extricate the tractor. The last thing Lanny saw was Leo D slowly sinking into the muddy
2 CONC  waters, with large veins sticking out of his neck. That may have been the demise of his farmering pursuits.    \par     \par One story from Denny's youth has stayed with us. While living in Riverside, California, Denny got lost o
2 CONC ne day. It seems he decided to hide in the car in the back of the car and see if his Dad really went to work everyday. (He did!!! Duh!~) Anyway, Sabina missed him and searched frantically for hours before calling to Paul at work, 
2 CONC who eventually discovered Denny in hiding.    \par This was not the first time he had disappeared. While living in Scobey, he was found many times squatting in the hen house. He always had the look of anticipation on his face, but
2 CONC  could never let the hens know that nothing came of it, so he would squawk and rise anyway. His "results" were never eggs.   }
