2 CONT https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/92403648/aagot-taxdahl
2 CONT
2 CONT Services will be held at 2 p.m. today (Thursday) in Saron Church south of town for Mrs. Jesper Taxdahl, long-time resident here who died Monday in a Fargo hospital. Rev. R. S. Lunde will officiate, assisted by Rev. K. Wuflestad.
2 CONT The former Aagot Johnson was born December 12, 1877, at Stavanger, Norway. She came to Minnesota in 1882 and to the Cooperstown area in 1883. She was married to Mr. Taxdahl December 12, 1900.
2 CONT Surviving are Mr. Taxdahl, three sons, Ernest of Revere, N.D., Orville of Hannaford, N.D. and Rev. Albert of Grafton, N. D.; three daughters, Neva and Mrs. Roy Wathe of Revere and Mrs. A. M. Selness of Rugby, N.D.; 15 grandchildre
2 CONC n; four sisters, Mrs. Sereina Holland of Binford, N.D., Mrs. Dorothea Larson of Hannaford, Mrs. Inge Anderson of Langdon, N.D., and Mrs. Chris Seldal of Cooperstown, and a brother, Hans Froiland of Cooperstown.
2 CONT Published in the Griggs County Sentinel-Courier, Cooperstown, North Dakota, April 28, 1949.
2 CONT
2 CONT Born Aagot Ellingsdatter to parents Elling Jonassen and Martha Dorthea Omundsdatter. Her family emigrated to the USA in 1882.
2 CONT
2 CONT On December 12, 1900, Aagot married Jesper Taxdahl at Cooperstown, North Dakota. To the union were born seven children: Ernest, Neva, Myrtle, Hilda, Albert, Judith and Orville Taxdahl.
2 CONT
2 CONT Aagot died on April 25, 1949 at St. Lukes Hospital in Fargo, North Dakota.
2 CONT Inscription
2 CONT Mother
2 CONT
