2 CONT https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/92403386/amelia_seke-seldal
2 CONT
2 CONT Funeral services were held Tuesday in Bethlehem Evangelical Free Church for Mrs. Christian (Amelia) Seldal, who died Saturday in the hospital here. Rev. Richard Haglund officiated at the funeral.
2 CONT Amelia Johnson, daughter of Mr. and Mrs. Elling Johnson, was born in Norway January 23, 1880. When she was two years old she came with her parents by covered wagon to Griggs County. They settled on the Froiland farm in a sod shant
2 CONC y. She had lived in this area ever since.
2 CONT Her marriage to Christian Seldal took place February 12, 1900 in Cooperstown. He died in 1955.
2 CONT Surviving are one son, Walter, Auburn, Wash.; six daughters, Mrs. C. M. (Irma) Lunde, Oregon City, Oregon; Mrs. S. I. (Dorothy) Allen, Crosby, N. D., Mrs. M. L. (Inga) Stringer, Great Falls, Mont.; Mrs. Henry (Alien) Wallestrom, D
2 CONC enver, Colo.; Mrs. Wilson (Ruth) Forbes, Bremerton, Wash.; and Mrs. V. C. (Myrtle Rose) Citron, Seattle, Wash.; one sister, Mrs. Inga Anderson, Minneapolis, Minn., and 19 grandchildren and 25 great-grandchildren.
2 CONT Quam-Plaisted Funeral Homes.
2 CONT Published in the Griggs County Sentinel-Courier, Cooperstown, North Dakota, August 19, 1965.
2 CONT Submitted by Dennis C. Olson #48363213
2 CONT
