1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Serine Olava Norheim Brosten was born February 27, 1897,  on Kylles in Hoyland, Norway.  Her father was Sven Omundson Norheim.  Her mother was Gunnhild Forland.   Her father was a farmer  and the sheriff of Time, N
2 CONC orway.  He was married three times.  Her half brothers and sisters were:  Anna Malena (Malla),  Omund (Omen),  Anna,  Sven,  Signe Bergitte,  Johannes,  Marta Dorthea,  Tonnes (Tony).  Serine was the youngest in the family. After 
2 CONC her schooling,  Serine worked at a clothing factory in Figgjo, Norway.  She met Peter Brosten when he was in Norway for a visit.  She emigrated to America on the ship,  Stavangerfjord, landing in New York on Sept. 25, 1923.  She w
2 CONC ent to Enga Espeland’s at Sidney, Montana.  She was twenty-six years old when she married Peter Brosten on November 28, 1923, in Sidney, Montana. Serine had hazel eyes,  dark brown hair,  was 5 feet 7 inches,  weighed up to 145 po
2 CONC unds. She was an exceptionally good cook,  and was well known throughout the world for it.  When the Sidney boys in the service were homesick,  they would reminisce about Serine’s good cooking. Serine was impulsive.  Her impulsive
2 CONC ness often unintentionally got her into comical situations, such as the time she thought she had telephoned a bachelor friend to invite him to dinner.  Instead her pastor and his family arrived for dinner! She was a great walker. 
2 CONC  She was always in control when meeting emergencies. In 1931 when Peter died,  the country was in the depths of the depression.  Serine displayed great courage and determination in raising her three small daughters alone on the ra
2 CONC nch.  She hung onto the homestead and it is still in the family. During WWII,  Serine worked for two years  as a welder in the shipyards at Vancouver, Washington.   She cooked at the Sidney Hospital for 15 years. She made her firs
2 CONC t trip back to visit Norway in 1949  by ship.  After that  she made a second trip by ship  and three trips by airplane. Serine always had good health.  She had a Norheim characteristic of tapping fingers.  She became a US citizen 
2 CONC in 1932. Serine died on August 30, 1988 at the age of 91.  She is buried at Sidney Cemetery in Sidney, Montana
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Høyland Gards - og Ættesoge 1500 - 1900, s. 251 nr. 39k, Serine Olava, g. m. Per Pederson Bråstein (Bråstein 67. c).
